<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2">
  <Document>
    <name>💨 LIVE WIND</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<p><b>Legend</b><br><img src="https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/wind/legend.png" width="600" alt="legend"><br>WIND — BEAUFORT SCALE (colors follow force, dark purple = Force 12 only):<br/><b>F0</b> — Calm (0–0.99 kt)<br/><b>F1</b> — Light air (1–3 kt)<br/><b>F2</b> — Light breeze (4–6 kt)<br/><b>F3</b> — Gentle breeze (7–10 kt)<br/><b>F4</b> — Moderate breeze (11–16 kt)<br/><b>F5</b> — Fresh breeze (17–21 kt)<br/><b>F6</b> — Strong breeze (22–27 kt)<br/><b>F7</b> — High wind (28–33 kt)<br/><b>F8</b> — Gale (34–40 kt)<br/><b>F9</b> — Strong gale (41–47 kt)<br/><b>F10</b> — Storm (48–55 kt)<br/><b>F11</b> — Violent storm (56–63 kt)<br/><b>F12</b> — Hurricane-force (≥64 kt)<br/>Maximum this run: <b>47 kt</b> (Beaufort 6). Full basin coverage: GLWU over water, HRRR 10 m fill over land. Arrows point where the air moves.</p><p>This entry auto-refreshes from the live overlay (source: NOAA/NCEP Great Lakes Wave Unstructured v2.1 (GLWUv2.1, WAVEWATCH III) — UGRD/VGRD surface analysis over water + NOAA/NCEP HRRR 3 km 10 m wind analysis as land/background fill (full basin rectangle, same footprint as Live Leaf Color)).</p><p>Turn on/off independently of the ice, wave and temperature layers. Add this file once; new source cycles appear automatically.</p><p><i>Not endorsed by NOAA.</i></p>]]></description>
    <NetworkLink>
      <name>💨 LIVE WIND — auto-refresh</name>
      <Link>
        <href>https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/kml/live/Great_Lakes_Live_Wind.kml</href>
        <refreshMode>onInterval</refreshMode>
        <refreshInterval>900</refreshInterval>
      </Link>
    </NetworkLink>
  </Document>
</kml>
